  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Derna Libya: Promoting The Participation Of Flood-affected Populations In The Humanitarian Response And Recovery Process</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to enable the direct participation of flood-affected communities in Derna in the humanitarian response and support their economic recovery. It seeks to empower communities and affected populations to participate in recovery and response efforts/activities. Through the project, the community resource mobile teams will be supported to improve access to information, and stakeholders&apos; capacity on Camp Coordination and Camp Management (CCCM) and Urban Displacement Out of Camp (UDOC) approach will be enhanced. In addition, the project will provide in-kind grants to support the recovery of Micro and small enterprises (MSEs) impacted by the floods.</narrative>
  </description>
